From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 04:41:35 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] VR true stereo: each eye path traced with its own view state

V7 (ADR 0198): with RTXVR_QUALITY_TRUE_STEREO and Ray Reconstruction, the
frame is path traced once per eye instead of warping one centre view.

- rtx_vr_eye.h: the eye the render thread is tracing (-1 centre, 0 left,
  1 right). The left eye keeps the default view state; the right eye's
  Resources, ReSTIR GI, Ray Reconstruction, NRC and SHaRC are a second set
  in DxvkObjects, selected by the existing accessors, so every pass and
  shader runs unchanged and each eye's histories advance once a frame.
  The right eye's Resources reads the frame's TLAS, noise, sky probe and
  matte from the default state.
- CameraManager: each eye's camera stands in for Main while that eye is
  traced; both follow the centre camera once a frame from the eye's offset
  and its own off-centre frustum (vrmath::eyeToCentreView, eyeProjection,
  unit-tested against the warp's eye rays).
- RtxContext::injectRTX traces one view per call of a local pass chain:
  the centre, or each eye in turn. The sky's integrators and the froxel
  volumetrics run once, on the centre camera; each eye fits the aerial
  perspective volume to its own frustum and keeps its own cloud history;
  auto exposure adapts once, from the left eye.
- RtxVr copies each eye's picture into its eye image and submits as before;
  the right eye writes no timestamps, so the profile's total covers both.
- The NRC library starts with the first context and stops with the last,
  so each eye's cache can exist at once.
